{"title":"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive 5-digit odd integers are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Palindrome\" title=\"Palindrome\">palindromes</a>?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The units digit must be odd, and the ten-thousands digit must be equal to the units digit. So there are 5 possible choices there. Then there are ten choices for the tens and hundreds digits, but the thousands digit is fixed. Therefore there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/c/4dc901f3f8e8dd1d6c05569e9f9e74e43ce56339.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 10=\\boxed{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"23\" /> 5-digit odd palindromes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a hr